<h1>Visa Financial Analysis (2023-2025)</h1>

<h2>Objective</h2>

<p>
The purpose of this project was to evaluate Visa's financial performance,
business model, and growth prospects using publicly available annual reports.
</p>

<h2>Business Overview</h2>

<p>
Visa operates one of the world's largest digital payment networks.
Unlike banks, Visa does not lend money directly. Instead, it earns
revenue by facilitating transactions between consumers, merchants,
and financial institutions.
</p>

<h2>Revenue Analysis</h2>

<p>
Revenue increased from $32.7 billion in 2023 to $40.0 billion in 2025.
This growth reflects increasing transaction activity and continued
adoption of digital payments.
</p>

<h2>What Interested Me</h2>

<p>
The most interesting aspect of Visa's business model is that it benefits
from transaction growth without assuming direct credit risk.
</p>

<h2>Conclusion</h2>

<p>
Visa appears to be a high-quality business with strong profitability,
network effects, and long-term growth opportunities.
</p>

